  "Id": 1653,
  "Title": "AKU faculty awarded Sitara-i-Imtiaz",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Professor Muhammad Anwar Waqar has been awarded the Sitara-i-Imtiaz.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>Professor Muhammad Anwar Waqar has been awarded the Sitara-i-Imtiaz by the president of Pakistan. </p><p>Professor Waqar, the Akbarali Bandeali Professor and Chair of Biochemistry, joined AKU in 1986 to head the department of biochemistry. He has been a leading figure in the field of molecular biology for many years and is best known for his work in the area of DNA structure and function. </p><p>Attributing his scientific inspiration to the revolution in DNA technology, Dr Waqar said that \"an understanding of molecular biology and nucleic acids sequencing offered an exciting new world of endless possibilities to me with far reaching consequences.\"</p>",
